@gfr-g we tried that design in prior stacks like ASP.NET 4.x and Microsoft.Owin, it had its own tradeoffs. Regardless, that's not a design point we can change at this point without breaking all the current users.

And yes, it should be possible to wrap the `IHttpUpgradeFeature` similar to how logging wraps the response body today. When UpgradeAsync is called that would trigger the same response header logging as writing to the response body does. We would not want to capture any of the actual websocket traffic.
https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/blob/f08285d0b6918fbb2b485d97f4e411dc9ea9a94f/src/Http/Http.Features/src/IHttpUpgradeFeature.cs#L9

@Tratcher thank you very much for your answer but, unfortunately, I think I'm missing something very obvious because I wasn't able to figure out exactly what you mean. 

This part: "And yes, it should be possible to wrap the IHttpUpgradeFeature similar to how logging wraps the response body today. When UpgradeAsync is called that **would trigger the same response header logging as writing to the response body does**." makes me believe there's an actual system in place that immediately logs the response headers when the response body is written to. I failed to find this wrapping mechanism in the source code and I also failed to make it work with a simple example like this that I believe should show what I think you meant with the sentence above

```
[...]

app.UseHttpLogging();
app.Use(async (context, next) =>
{
	await next();
	await Task.Delay(10000);
});

app.Run(async (context) =>
{
        // not really necessary 
	context.Response.StatusCode = 200;
	context.Response.Headers.ContentType = "text/html; charset=UTF-8";

        // write to the body
	await context.Response.WriteAsync("test");
});

[...]

```

I'm not able to see any response headers being logged (I used the console provider and the event source provider) while the middleware pipeline is waiting for the ten seconds delay.

Would you mind to please elaborate further your proposal?
